KNOWNBUG
partial-assignment-before-non-constant-index3.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.s\.hi == 4'b1111\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The assignment to s.arr[i] is rewritten into an assignment to the
whole of s, using the value of s before the assignment. That value is
taken to be the current-state value of s whenever no single recorded
slice covers all of s, and hence the preceding blocking assignment to
s.hi is lost.
